RISC3D test kit 21 (prototype, 14 November 2026)
================================================

Kit 20 showed the Track test drawn right through RISC3D (18 of 76,800
pixels differ by a shade from Linux's own, from texture filtering), so
what TORCS draws wrongly (details missing, textures not applied) is
something TORCS does that Track doesn't. This kit's rol-3d (0.10, in
riscos-risc3d 0.10-1) can log what goes wrong while TORCS runs.

Steps
-----
 1. Copy RISC3DTest to HardDisc4 (unzip it there, replacing kit 20).
 2. In RiSH's Root shell:
      apt-get install /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/riscos-risc3d_0.10-1_arm64.deb
    It restarts rol-3d itself. Don't reload the modules.
 3. In RiSH's Root shell, the tests with Linux's Mesa directly:
      sh /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/linux-tests
    Then double-click Textures: TexResults should match TexLinuxResults
    line for line (the multitexture and big-texture drawing TORCS does).
    Then, in RiSH's Root shell:
      sh /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/check on
 4. Run TORCS through RISC3D: start a race, drive for half a minute or
    so (past 600 frames if you can), then quit TORCS.
 5. In RiSH's Root shell:
      sh /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/check off
    and copy /riscos/3d/log.txt to the Mac.
    (The check makes TORCS a little slower, and TORCS's own glGetError
    sees no errors while it's on.)

Also useful
-----------
 * TORCS both ways of passing arrays (from kit 20):
      sh /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/uploads buffers   (0.7's way)
      sh /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/uploads memory    (the default)

